    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0509" n="1243" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1243"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-15"><hi rendition="#italic">April 15, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 29.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 501.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 402, of the 30th ultimo,
                    has been received, and I have the honor to inform you that the result has
                    justified my conclusion not to send Mr. Jewett to Bitlis. I chose rather to rely
                    for security on the promise of the Porte, made on my emphatic demand for a
                    telegram to every governor and military commander in Asia Minor to enforce
                    respect and protection for our citizens. An increased feeling of security in the
                    interior shows that the order was sent.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
